artifact.self_contained_problem:
A feedforward neural network with rectified linear unit (ReLU) activation is a function $f:\mathbb{R}^n\to\mathbb{R}^m$ obtained by composing finitely many affine maps $x\mapsto Ax+b$ (with real matrices $A$ and vectors $b$) with the coordinatewise ReLU nonlinearity $\sigma(x)=\max(x,0)$, possibly followed by a final affine output map. The (max-plus) tropical semiring is $(\mathbb{R}\cup\{-\infty\},\oplus,\odot)$ with $a\oplus b=\max(a,b)$ and $a\odot b=a+b$. A tropical polynomial in $n$ variables is a finite expression $p(x)=\max_{i}(\langle a_i,x\rangle+c_i)$ with $a_i\in\mathbb{Z}^n$ and $c_i\in\mathbb{R}$; a tropical signomial allows $a_i\in\mathbb{R}^n$. A tropical rational (signomial) map is a coordinatewise difference of two tropical (signomial) polynomials. 

Establish a complete correspondence between tropical geometry and neural networks built from ReLU activations and affine maps. Concretely, give a precise bijective dictionary between:

(i) the class of functions computable by feedforward ReLU networks (with real weights) and the class of tropical rational signomial maps;
(ii) architectural invariants of the network (depth, width, number of neurons, weight integrality) and tropical-geometric invariants (Newton polytopes, number of monomials, degrees of the numerator and denominator polynomials, mixed volumes, normal fans);
(iii) the decision boundary and linear-region decomposition of the network and the tropical hypersurface and polyhedral subdivision associated with the corresponding tropical rational map.

The correspondence should be functorial in the sense that composition, addition, and maximum of networks correspond to the appropriate tropical operations, and should allow translation of expressivity bounds (e.g., number of linear regions) into combinatorial bounds on polytopes and vice versa.

